<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= meta.title %></title>
  <meta name="description" content="<%= meta.description %>">
  <link rel="canonical" href="<%= meta.canonical %>">
  <meta property="og:title" content="<%= meta.title %>">
  <meta property="og:description" content="<%= meta.description %>">
  <meta property="og:image" content="<%= meta.ogImage %>">
  <meta property="og:url" content="<%= meta.canonical %>">
  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,300;0,9..40,400;0,9..40,500;0,9..40,600;1,9..40,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/theme.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/guides.css">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Ozarks Outdoor Adventures",
    "description": "<%= meta.description %>",
    "image": "<%= meta.ogImage %>",
    "url": "<%= meta.canonical %>",
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "OzarkRoost", "url": "<%= baseUrl %>" },
    "datePublished": "2026-06-22",
    "dateModified": "2026-09-17"
  }
  </script>
</head>
<body>
<%- include('../partials/guide-nav') %>
<header class="guide-hero">
  <img class="guide-hero__img" src="<%= heroImages.ozarksAdventures %>" alt="Kayakers on an Ozark river through autumn canyon">
  <div class="guide-hero__overlay"></div>
  <div class="guide-hero__content">
    <p class="guide-hero__eyebrow">Destination Guide</p>
    <h1>Ozarks Outdoor Adventures</h1>
    <p class="guide-hero__sub">Real destinations, official sources, and practical trip-planning notes.</p>
    <a href="/listings" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Find Your Ozarks Stay</a>
  </div>
</header>
<article class="guide-body">
  <section class="guide-section">
    <div class="guide-prose">
      <p>This guide focuses on real Ozarks destinations that can be checked against government or first-party sources. Conditions, closures, water levels, trail status and operating schedules can change, so verify current information with the destination or land manager before traveling.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-section">
    <h2>Outdoor Adventures</h2>
    <ol class="guide-numbered">
      <li>
        <h3>Hike to Hemmed-In Hollow Falls</h3>
        <p>The National Park Service describes the falls as nearly 210 feet high and the highest waterfall between the Rockies and the Appalachians. The Compton route is extremely steep and strenuous, descends nearly 1,400 feet, and should be planned as a full-day wilderness hike. The falls flow after substantial rain.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Plan a Buffalo National River Float</h3>
        <p>The National Park Service lists river accesses including Ponca, Steel Creek, Kyles Landing, Pruitt, Hasty and Buffalo Point. Float difficulty and timing depend on river conditions, so check current NPS conditions and access information before launching.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Visit Blanchard Springs Caverns</h3>
        <p>Blanchard Springs Caverns is a developed living cave in the Ozark-St. Francis National Forests. Forest Service status pages can change, so check the current site status and tour information before making the drive.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Explore Whitaker Point / Hawksbill Crag</h3>
        <p>The Forest Service identifies Whitaker Point (Hawksbill Crag) as a trailhead providing access to the Upper Buffalo Wilderness. Check Forest Service alerts, parking information and road conditions before heading out.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Explore Beaver Lake</h3>
        <p>The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers lists Beaver Lake at about 28,299 surface acres with roughly 490 miles of natural shoreline and multiple public parks and campgrounds. Boating, fishing, swimming and other water recreation are available at designated areas.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Fish the White River</h3>
        <p>The White River is a major Arkansas fishing corridor. Before fishing, check Arkansas Game and Fish Commission regulations, licenses, access information and current conditions rather than relying on a generic catch or difficulty claim.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Hike the Ozark Highlands Trail</h3>
        <p>The Forest Service describes the Ozark Highlands Trail as a 165-mile corridor from Lake Fort Smith State Park to the Buffalo River. Trail conditions and access can vary, so use current Forest Service information when planning a section hike.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Watch Elk Around Ponca</h3>
        <p>Arkansas Game and Fish Commission materials identify the Buffalo River area as important elk habitat and note that late September and early October are a strong period for viewing and photographing elk. Observe from appropriate public viewing areas and follow wildlife rules.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Visit Steel Creek</h3>
        <p>Steel Creek is a Buffalo National River access and campground area beneath the river bluffs. The National Park Service provides current maps, access information and campground details; check those resources before your trip.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>See the Ozark Mountain Views Near Jasper</h3>
        <p>The Jasper and Buffalo River region offers scenic overlooks, river country and access to hiking destinations. Build the trip around verified trail and access information rather than relying on unverified mileage, height or “best view” claims.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-section">
    <h2>Where to Stay</h2>
    <div class="guide-prose">
      <p>Use the OzarkRoost lodging directory as a starting point, then verify availability, amenities, pricing and property details directly with the lodging provider before booking.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-cta-group">
      <a href="/listings" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Browse Ozarks stays</a>
      <a href="/adventures" class="guide-cta">Explore verified destinations &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>
<%- include('../partials/affiliate-widget', { bundle: 'adventure' }) %>
<%- include('../partials/affiliate-widget', { bundle: 'gear' }) %>
</article>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
<script>(function(){var slug="ozarkroost";if(!slug)return;var vid=localStorage.getItem('polsia_vid');if(!vid){vid='xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'.replace(/[xy]/g,function(c){var r=Math.random()*16|0;return(c==='x'?r:(r&0x3|0x8)).toString(16);});localStorage.setItem('polsia_vid',vid);}new Image().src='https://polsia.com/api/beacon/pixel?s='+encodeURIComponent(slug)+'&v='+encodeURIComponent(vid);})();</script>
</body>
</html>
